    "A standing instruction for purchase threshold approval coverage needs a limit and an expiry, and the operations lead should confirm it is still current. Record rejected and deferred requests as well as approvals. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. In the purchase threshold approval coverage queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception. In this review, the coding sheet is logged on the assistant placement so the client operations manager can rebuild the measured rate from the assignment and workforce record.",
